--[==[
NEXUS HUB — ONE-FILE EXPERIENCE DEVELOPER DASHBOARD (GUARDED LIFECYCLE)
Build: 2026-10-25-NEXUS-HUB-v3.1-MINIDOCK-DRAG-SMOOTHING
Install LocalScript: StarterPlayer > StarterPlayerScripts (Roblox Studio).
When the runtime exposes readfile/writefile, settings and named configs autosave in one local JSON file.
In standard Roblox Studio, true cross-session persistence still requires a server DataStore Script.
Then press Play and use Insert to show/hide the menu.

This single LocalScript provides client-side developer/testing features:
- Separate Player Visuals and NPC Visuals categories with independent labels, health bars, boxes, tracers, skeleton, look direction, colors, distance limits, fade controls and off-screen edge indicators
- Separate NPC Aim category with independent FOV, smoothing, target part and visibility checks; a shared aim palette styles FOV and diagnostic markers
- Team recognition and team counts
- FOV circle, crosshair, target part, visibility/team checks and frame-rate-independent camera aim smoothing
- Fly, walk/jump boost, bunny hop, infinite jump and local noclip test mode
- Local lighting options, camera FOV, FPS, player selection, spectating and local teleport tests
- 12-language GUI, smooth cancellable tab/button animations, animation-speed/reduced-motion/scale controls, live debug HUD, diagnostics, spawn markers, low-graphics mode, presets, named profiles, JSON import/export, vertical HP bars

Startup displays a release-history panel and a version badge; the same history can be reopened from Overview. The GUI includes configurable keyboard binds. ServerHop UI is included, but actual cross-server teleport requires a companion server Script in ServerScriptService; Roblox teleporting is server-authoritative.
Persistence mode: filesystem autosave when readfile/writefile are available; otherwise uses the optional server DataStore bridge. Standard Roblox LocalScripts cannot write directly to the user's disk or access DataStoreService.
Server-authoritative invincibility and wallbang still require server weapon/gameplay integration.
]==]


